@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-10
@reviewed: 2026-10-15

Feature: Static Host Provisioning Script Generator
  "Renders the idempotent provisioning script for a static site (apex domain or subdomain): a mason-owned, group-readable web root, Caddy group access, and a Mason-owned static Caddy snippet imported once. Apex domains also get a www→apex redirect. No share scaffolding, no user/key creation."

  Provides:
    - setup.SiteInitParams @source("symbol:SiteInitParams")
    - setup.SiteInitScript @source("symbol:SiteInitScript")

  Consumes:
    - config.Target
    - setup.writeCaddyGroupAccessBlock
    - setup.writeCaddyImportBlock
    - setup.writeCaddyReloadBlock

  Invariants:
    - SiteInitScript MUST be a deterministic, pure function of its params (same input, same script)
    - The script MUST be idempotent for the web root, the snippet file, and the Caddyfile import line
    - The Caddy snippet MUST be a static file_server vhost and MUST NOT include the share store's /objects/* private-prefix matcher
    - The Caddy snippet MUST 404 every dotfile path (`path */.*`) except /.well-known/*, before file_server and after any SPA try_files
    - Apex vs subdomain MUST be auto-detected via the Public Suffix List, overridable by DomainMode ("apex"/"subdomain")
    - An apex domain MUST be served from the bare apex and (unless NoWWW) MUST add a permanent www→apex redirect; a www-prefixed base_url MUST normalize to the same apex result
    - A subdomain MUST be served verbatim with no www redirect block
    - The script MUST NOT create users, groups, or SSH keys, and MUST assume the mason service user already exists
    - The script MUST NOT emit share-tree scaffolding (objects/, s/, .mason/)
    - The web root MUST be group-readable (2750, mason-owned) so Caddy can serve it
    - A reload MUST be gated by `caddy validate`; without Reload the script only prints the manual steps
    - The script MUST never rewrite the main Caddyfile beyond appending the single import line
    - A missing web root or site address MUST return an error and produce no script
    - --spa MUST add a try_files fallback to /index.html; default off

  OutOfScope:
    - Share tree scaffolding and the private-prefix 404 snippet (remote-init / future share-init)
    - Service user, group, and deploy-key creation (remote-init)
    - Executing the script over SSH (cli site-init owns --apply)
    - rsync / deploy of the site contents

  Scenario (happy-path): Plain static host
    Given a target with a base_url and deploy.remote_path
    When SiteInitScript renders
    Then it creates the web root, grants Caddy group access, writes a plain static snippet, and imports it once

  Scenario (happy-path): Apex domain with www redirect
    Given an apex base_url (example.com or www.example.com)
    When SiteInitScript renders
    Then it serves the bare apex and adds a permanent www.example.com → apex redirect block

  Scenario (edge): SPA fallback
    Given SPA is true
    When SiteInitScript renders
    Then the snippet adds try_files {path} /index.html before file_server

  Scenario (edge): Host and root overrides
    Given Host and Root are set and the target lacks base_url / remote_path
    When SiteInitScript renders
    Then the overrides supply the site address and web root

  Scenario (negative): Missing web root or site address
    Given a target without deploy.remote_path/--root or without base_url/--host
    When SiteInitScript renders
    Then it returns an error and produces no script
